Author: Seul Lee <ftk3187@athena.athena.research.northwestern.edu>
Date:   Mon Oct 19 22:44:43 2026 -0500

    P136b: D11-D13, figure entities by conditions, fallback activities, prompt NK/claim/run definitions, units, prices
    
    compile.py: D11 quote against the record's element and the element ids it mentions,
    texts joined; D12 a variables quantity outside the enum -> null (variables_unmapped,
    record kept); D13 a gold model row without a value matches a model row on a shared
    element (diff and audit). figures.json: one entity per distinct conditions dict;
    the conditions all entities of a simulation share go once on it; row type by the
    curve's kind (simulated -> model, read_from_figure -> observation); evidence ids
    de-duplicated. Fallbacks: a simulation activity (how inferred) for simulated curves
    pass 0 gives none for; a run under the recipe (how inferred) when pass 0 names none
    and reactant_A / deposition_temperature settings exist. Dedupe: the same row again
    from the same element(s) with the same label is dropped (D5 kept); multi-element
    evidence merged as sets. normalize(): \times -> ×. Step k: the printed value text,
    then label and term, left out when a statement still repeats eight words.
    units.yaml: "x" for 1; normalized_thickness += "normalized thickness"; ontology.yaml
    header hash 7a72429b. pass1 RULES: the four NK reasons, claim (with a full claim
    example), reactor/instrument value_text = the name. pass0 INSTRUCTION: run,
    simulation, specimen defined; one example list from another dev paper's gold tree.
    prices.csv: google gemini-3.8-flash 0.75 / 3.75 per Mtok (third-party listings).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

